  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#spastic_tragedy_slur",
  "@type": "BackgroundKnowledge",
  "instance_name": "spastic_tragedy_slur",
  "label": "Derogatory slur targeting individuals with physical or developmental disabilities",
  "description": "The term 'spastic' is a historically offensive slur used to demean individuals with cerebral palsy or other movement disorders. The phrase 'spastic tragedy' combines this slur with the concept of a 'tragedy' to dehumanize and mock the perceived physical clumsiness or lack of coordination of the child. This is a form of ableism, which involves mocking or stigmatizing people based on their physical or developmental characteristics.",
